# Copy this file to .env.local for local dev, or set the same key in your
# Vercel project's Environment Variables for the deployed build.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL is read server-side by pages/api/proxy/[...path].ts
# (the browser never talks to the backend directly, so despite the
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix nothing sensitive here reaches the client bundle —
# it's just the backend's URL, kept public for historical/simplicity reasons).
#
# Local dev (backend running via `uvicorn` on your machine):
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
#
# Once the backend is deployed (e.g. to Render), set this to that URL instead:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://emotionless-executioner-api.onrender.com
#
# Backend API keys — deliberately NOT NEXT_PUBLIC_*. Only
# pages/api/proxy/[...path].ts reads these (server-side), and it picks
# whichever one matches the visitor's session role. Must match the
# backend's API_KEY / API_KEY_READONLY exactly (see backend/.env.example).
# API_KEY=
# API_KEY_READONLY=
#
# Login gate (frontend-only, server-side — never sent to the browser).
# Leave all unset for local dev to skip the login page entirely.
# SITE_PASSWORD=
# SITE_PASSWORD_READONLY=
# SESSION_SECRET=
